Binary Search AlgorithmThis algorithm only work on sorted data. It divides the array into two equal halves and compares the target value with the middle element. If the target matches the middle element, it returns the mid index. If the target is less than the middle element, the algorithm works on the left half of the array. If the target is more than the middle element, the algorithm works on the right half of the array.
<jupyter_code>
def binary_search(array, target):
    low = 0
    high = len(array) - 1
    while low <= high:
        mid = (low + high) // 2
        if array[mid] == target:
            return mid
        elif array[mid] < target:
            low = mid + 1
        else:
            high = mid - 1
    return -1

# Testing the function
